    {
      "id": "5cf37c3b-b128-4abd-9f49-1018e2deb4d2",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 314,
      "shortId": "GFFU8",
      "priority": 8,
      "shortName": "correct-the-published-document",
      "title": "Correct the published documents so the examples match what the model can actually do",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Closes gaps 7 and 8, and reconciles the docs with whatever T1-T7 changed. DO THIS LAST — the\ncorrections depend on the decisions taken in T6 (Row naming) and T7 (colour).\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT COSMETIC\ndocs/chrome-and-ui.md is the file a plugin author reads first. Its examples are currently\nunbuildable in spirit: they use settings and widgets the model does not have. A reader cannot tell\nwhich lines are real. The document does carry a \"STATUS: DESIGN — target Phase 9, NOT yet available\"\nbanner (docs/chrome-and-ui.md:3-8), which excuses the SDK types not existing — it does not excuse\nexamples that will still be wrong after the SDK ships.\n\nTHE TWO OUTRIGHT ERRORS (no native equivalent exists — these are doc bugs, not gaps)\n1. `Panel::new().title(\"Hello\")` — docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 1 and README.md's Plugins section.\n   There is no Panel widget. `WidgetKind::Panel` realizes to a plain `Surface` (realize.rs:129-131,\n   whose comment states \"No dedicated `Panel` widget — a bare panel is a plain `Surface`\"), and\n   `Surface` has no title (surface.rs — only `new`/`row`/`column`). `Card::new(title)` is the titled\n   container. Either rewrite the example onto `Card`, or add a title to Panel — but do not leave a\n   title on a thing that has none.\n2. `Label::new(..).variant(Variant::Muted)` — docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 2. No `Label` variant\n   exists natively and `ViewVariant` has no Muted (view.rs:169-176). Resolution depends on T7: if\n   colour tokens are wired, rewrite as a token colour; if T7 removes the colour value, drop the\n   muted styling from the example entirely.\n\nALSO RECONCILE (settings that WILL exist once this phase lands, so the examples become true)\n- `Column::new().padding(10)` — real after T2.\n- `Input::new(..).placeholder(\"filter…\")` — real after T4. Note the example writes\n  `Input::new(\"filter\")`, which reads like a name but is positioned as a value; make the example\n  unambiguous about which is which, since `text` is the value and `name` is the form key.\n- `Scroll::vertical()` — real after T4, and worth showing the two-axis form too, since that was the\n  capability nobody could reach.\n- `Separator::new()` — real after T5.\n- `Row::new()…on_press(..)` for a clickable table row — real after T6, spelled however T6 decided.\n\nFILES TO UPDATE — all of them, in one pass\n- docs/chrome-and-ui.md (examples 1, 2, 3 + the \"What's shipped vs planned\" section at line 268).\n- README.md — the \"Plugins (Planned)\" section (README.md:30 in the contents, the section itself\n  further down) carries the same Panel/title example.\n- docs/chrome-and-ui.md §2.6.1 (line ~252) and §2.6.2 (line ~340) — both sketch the SDK\n  with `.padding(12)` and a titled Panel.\n- docs/widgets.md + the props-by-kind table in view.rs's rustdoc, if any earlier task left them\n  behind.\n\nONE MORE FIX — A STALE POINTER\ndocs/chrome-and-ui.md:7 tells the reader to \"Track progress under the `plugin-ui` and `plugin-08`\nphases in `BACKLOG.md`\". BACKLOG.md is stale and is NOT the source of truth — the planner is. Point\nreaders at the planner instead. (This is the correction that was owed to F003/P011/T008, whose docs\nare otherwise complete.)\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Every code example in the three documents uses only settings and widgets that exist after this\n  phase.\n- No document promises a titled Panel or a Label variant unless one was actually built.\n- The BACKLOG pointer is gone.\n- Re-read each example as a newcomer would and confirm nothing left in them is aspirational without\n  saying so.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-27 — commits a3485a6 (Panel), 5768cd3 (Part II examples), e5a3b56 (the source sweep), branch `feat/action-arg-declaration`. Showcase verified by the user. NOT pushed.\n\n## ⚠️ ONE RESERVATION LEFT OPEN BY THE USER — DO NOT LOSE THIS\n\nOn seeing the showcase: *\"showcase is ok. not sure the title position is what i expected but for now is ok.\"*\n\nSo `Panel`'s heading placement is **accepted provisionally, not approved**. As built it is the first child of a padding-10, gap-8 column: top-left, inside the padding, directly above the content, bold at font_scale 1.05. If a future session touches `Panel`, ask before assuming the current placement is settled — the user was asked what they expected instead and their answer governs.\n\n## THE USER'S DECISIONS THIS TASK APPLIED\n\n1. **The Panel title is real** — rather than rewriting the examples onto `Card`. \"add a title to panel, label use the new color prop. but the panel title should be tested in the showcase.\"\n2. **Part II's code examples get corrected in place** — the user pushed back on my leaving them: *\"should them be HStack and VStack now?\"* and *\"you have to update the docs, right? so if you find things that do not respect the current code you have to change / fix them.\"* The verbatim rule protects design *reasoning*, not identifiers that no longer compile.\n\n## WHAT SHIPPED\n\n**`Panel` is a real widget** (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/panel.rs). Titled section container; the difference from `Card` is presentation, not structure — a Card stands apart (padding 18, theme frame), a Panel is a slice of a region and is quiet by default. The heading is a real `Label` child per the composition rule, created up front and **hidden until a title is set**, so `title` works applied before OR after children — properties land after children are attached, and a widget whose setters depend on ordering is the bug. `title_signal()` retitles a mounted panel with no rebuild. `WidgetKind::Panel` stops sharing the `Surface` arm and takes `text` as its heading, like `Card`/`DockFrame`.\n\nTest `a_panel_titles_itself_whichever_order_it_is_built_in` covers both orders, the hidden header when untitled, and clearing a title back to empty. Showcase shows a titled and an untitled panel side by side.\n\n**Doc errors fixed (the two the task named, plus more found while fixing them):**\n- `Panel::new().title(\"Hello\")` against a widget with no title — chrome-and-ui.md example 1 + README. Now real.\n- `Label::new(..).variant(Variant::Heading)` (Part II §3) — `Label` has NO `variant` builder, ever. A heading is `size: header`.\n- `Variant::Danger` on a Button (Part II §3) — the vocabulary is Primary/Secondary/Destructive/Outline/Ghost/Link.\n- `Panel::new(\"docker.containers\")` — took an argument Panel does not have.\n- The serialized form in the same comment used `kind:\"Panel\"` / `kind:\"Row\"`; the model emits snake_case, so `kind:\"panel\"` / `kind:\"h_stack\"`.\n- `Theme::grid_ares()` (widgets.md) — never existed. Only `grid_tron()` is built in code; bundled themes are grid_tron/mocha/latte via `load_theme`, which falls back user file → bundled → grid_tron and never fails.\n- AGENTS.md's \"implemented catalog\" was missing Panel, Row, Item, ItemGroup, Grid, DockFrame, ChromeRegion, Tag.\n- `Column`/`Row` → `VStack`/`HStack` in every remaining example, both parts, plus docs/widgets.md's two mentions of the future typed builder.\n\n**Part II's header no longer claims to be unedited.** It now says the prose is verbatim and the code examples were corrected on 2026-07-27, with the reason. §21 gained rows for the Label and Button variants so the record of what was wrong survives the correction.\n\n## TWO ITEMS IN THE TASK WERE ALREADY DONE\n\nVerified, not fixed by me: `Label::new(..).variant(Variant::Muted)` is nowhere in the docs, and the stale `BACKLOG.md` progress pointer is gone — both removed by the 2026-07-26 consolidation.\n\n## THE SWEEP (how \"every example matches the code\" was actually checked)\n\nCross-checked all 97 distinct `Type::method(` calls in the code examples of chrome-and-ui.md, widgets.md, README.md, AGENTS.md and widget-architecture.md against the source, then every documented builder in widgets.md against its own widget's file. Three apparent mismatches were false positives worth recording so the next sweep does not re-derive them: `Row::child` and `MarkerGroup::child` come from the `Parent` trait, `IconButton::size` from `LayoutExt`. AGENTS.md's mention of `Intensity::glow_scale` describes its removal, not a promise.\n\n## GATE\n\n`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings; `cargo test --workspace` green across 20 suites; showcase builds and was run. No `cargo fmt`.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-27 — commits a3485a6 (Panel), 5768cd3 (Part II examples), e5a3b56 (source sweep), a5ac706 (the header rule). Branch `feat/action-arg-declaration`, not pushed.\n\n## CLOSED AS-IS BY THE USER, WITH THE PANEL HEADER AS BUILT\n\nThe user saw the first Panel and said *\"showcase is ok. not sure the title position is what i expected but for now is ok.\"* Rather than leave that as a \"for now\", they were given four concrete options and chose **a rule under the heading**, adding *\"like in the pane header we have in the app.\"*\n\nThe pane header could not be copied: it is a **marker bar plus a button cluster in a centred row** (`build_pane_header`, heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:733), with no titled band. So `a5ac706` builds the shape they picked — heading → rule → body — and they were told plainly it matches the shape, not that construction.\n\nTheir close: *\"close it as it is now. eventually a new task will handle a refactoring.\"* So the current Panel header is **accepted, and any further shaping is a future task's job** — not an open reservation on this one. If that task appears, the likely axes are the header's height, where the rule sits, and the title's weight.\n\n## THE USER'S DECISIONS THIS TASK APPLIED\n\n1. **The Panel title is real** — over rewriting the examples onto `Card`.\n2. **Part II's code examples get corrected in place.** The user pushed twice: *\"should them be HStack and VStack now?\"* then *\"you have to update the docs, right? so if you find things that do not respect the current code you have to change / fix them. Come on.\"* The verbatim rule protects design *reasoning*, not identifiers that no longer compile.\n\n## WHAT SHIPPED\n\n**`Panel` is a real widget** (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/panel.rs). A titled section container: heading, a `Separator` under it, then the body. The difference from `Card` is presentation, not structure — a Card stands apart (padding 18, theme frame), a Panel is a slice of a region and is quiet by default.\n\nThe heading and its rule are real composed children per the composition rule, created up front and **hidden together until a title is set** — so `title` works applied before OR after children (properties land after children attach), and an untitled panel draws neither a blank line nor a bare rule. `title_signal()` retitles a mounted panel with no rebuild. `WidgetKind::Panel` stops sharing the `Surface` arm and takes `text` as its heading, like `Card`/`DockFrame`.\n\nTest `a_panel_titles_itself_whichever_order_it_is_built_in` covers both orders, the hidden header+rule when untitled, and clearing a title back to empty. Showcase shows a titled and an untitled panel side by side.\n\n**Doc errors fixed** (the two the task named, plus more found while fixing them):\n- `Panel::new().title(\"Hello\")` against a widget with no title — chrome-and-ui.md example 1 + README.\n- `Label::new(..).variant(Variant::Heading)` (Part II §3) — `Label` has NO `variant` builder, ever. A heading is `size: header`.\n- `Variant::Danger` on a Button — the vocabulary is Primary/Secondary/Destructive/Outline/Ghost/Link.\n- `Panel::new(\"docker.containers\")` — an argument Panel does not take.\n- `kind:\"Panel\"` / `kind:\"Row\"` in a serialized-form comment — the model emits snake_case.\n- `Theme::grid_ares()` (widgets.md) — never existed. Only `grid_tron()` is built in code; bundled themes are grid_tron/mocha/latte via `load_theme`, which falls back user file → bundled → grid_tron.\n- AGENTS.md's \"implemented catalog\" was missing Panel, Row, Item, ItemGroup, Grid, DockFrame, ChromeRegion, Tag.\n- `Column`/`Row` → `VStack`/`HStack` in every remaining example, both parts, plus widgets.md's two mentions of the future typed builder.\n\n**Part II's header no longer claims to be unedited.** It says the prose is verbatim and the code examples were corrected 2026-07-27, with the reason. §21 gained rows for the Label and Button variants so the record survives the correction.\n\n## TWO ITEMS IN THE TASK WERE ALREADY DONE\n\nVerified, not fixed by me: `Label::new(..).variant(Variant::Muted)` is nowhere in the docs, and the stale `BACKLOG.md` pointer is gone — both removed by the 2026-07-26 consolidation.\n\n## THE SWEEP\n\nCross-checked all 97 distinct `Type::method(` calls in the code examples of chrome-and-ui.md, widgets.md, README.md, AGENTS.md and widget-architecture.md against the source, then every documented builder in widgets.md against its own widget's file. Three apparent mismatches were false positives, recorded so the next sweep does not re-derive them: `Row::child` and `MarkerGroup::child` come from the `Parent` trait, `IconButton::size` from `LayoutExt`. AGENTS.md's mention of `Intensity::glow_scale` describes its removal, not a promise.\n\n## GATE\n\nclippy 0 warnings; `cargo test --workspace` green across 20 suites; showcase builds and was run by the user. No `cargo fmt`.",
