    {
      "id": "eedbd3a5-22c8-4a8a-8e7a-3f9a1c470822",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 315,
      "shortId": "B5E92",
      "priority": 9,
      "shortName": "open-question-not-for-this-pha",
      "title": "Move the view model to its own crate + make realize callable from below heca",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "# ✅ DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-27 — LEVEL 2. START HERE, DO NOT RE-ASK.\n\n**Move the pure-data model out of the app into its own crate, AND make `realize` callable from\nbelow `heca`.** The user was given Level 1 / Level 2 / neither with an effort estimate and chose\nLevel 2: *\"go with level 2, record it in t009.\"*\n\n- **Level 1 (NOT enough, do not stop here):** move only `ViewNode` / `WidgetKind` / `PropValue` /\n  `Intent`. Buys a plugin author type-checking and completion for the tree they author. Buys\n  **nothing** for rendering — `realize` would still be stuck in `heca`.\n- **Level 2 (WHAT WAS CHOSEN):** the above **plus** abstracting `realize`'s three app couplings so\n  it can live and be called below `heca`. This is what makes a described tree renderable from the\n  showcase.\n\n## ✅ CRATE LAYOUT — DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-27 (step 3's open sub-question, now closed)\n\n**TWO crates.** Do not revisit.\n\n| Crate | Holds | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`heca-view`** | the model: `ViewNode`, `WidgetKind`, `PropValue`, `Intent`, `PropMap`, `ViewSize`, `ViewVariant`, `ViewAlign`, `Events` | **`serde` only** — no widget library, no renderer, no taffy |\n| **`heca-view-realize`** | `realize` + `FormBindings` + realize's ~1500-line test module | `heca-view`, `heca-grid-ui`, `heca-theme` |\n\nWhy two: the model crate staying dependency-free is what lets a WASM plugin depend on the\nvocabulary without compiling the thing that draws it. One crate would have dragged\n`heca-grid-ui` + taffy into every such dependant, which is reason 1 of this task lost.\n\n## WHY — two independent reasons, and the second is what decided it\n\n1. **A plugin author gets no editor help.** The model is inside the app binary crate; a plugin is a\n   separate program and cannot depend on it. (The original reason this task was written.)\n2. **The showcase cannot render a described tree at all** — and this bit three times in one day.\n   `heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs` sits BELOW `heca` in the crate graph, so it cannot call\n   `realize`. During F003/P017/T005 (Separator), T006 (Row) and T007 (appearance) the user could\n   not be shown the declarative half of any of them; each time the answer was \"I can't show you\n   this.\" The only production caller of `realize` is a modal body\n   (`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs:367`), so no described tree appears anywhere else in the running\n   app. **That is a verification gap on every future vocabulary task**, and the user verifies\n   rendering themselves — green tests are never verification for anything visual.\n\nThe user also asked separately whether `heca-grid-ui` could ship as a standalone UI crate. Answer:\nthe renderer is NOT the blocker (heca-grid-ui depends only on heca-core, heca-theme, taffy and its\nmacros — `Scene`, the draw-command list, lives in `heca-grid-ui/src/scene.rs`, so an embedder\nsupplies their own backend). `realize` being app-side IS the blocker, for the declarative path.\n\n## WHY THIS IS NOT THE FORBIDDEN THING\n\n`AGENTS.md` and `docs/widget-architecture.md` §5 reject `heca-grid-ui` owning `ViewNode`: it\ninverts the crate graph, and `ViewNode` cannot carry the closures/signals the native chrome needs.\nThat rule is about pushing the model **DOWN INTO the widget library**. A separate crate\n**ALONGSIDE** inverts nothing and is a different question. Do not treat the settled rule as having\nalready answered it — this task's original text says exactly that, and the user has now decided.\n\n# MEASUREMENTS (taken 2026-07-27 — do not re-derive)\n\n| Thing | Size / fact |\n|---|---|\n| `heca/src/chrome/view.rs` (the model) | **632 lines**. Imports are ONLY `serde::{Deserialize, Serialize}` and `std::collections::BTreeMap` — a clean lift, no app dependencies at all. |\n| `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs` | **2630 lines**, of which roughly **1500 is its `#[cfg(test)]` module**. Non-test body ≈ 1100 lines. |\n| `HintTargetRegistry` (heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:2579) | **7 fields/lines of struct**; methods `register`/`checkpoint`/`remove_range`/`get`. |\n| `FormBindings` (heca/src/chrome/realize.rs:58) | **6 lines**. Already local to realize.rs — moves with it. |\n| `InteractionIntent` inside non-test `realize` | **7 real use sites** (plus doc comments). |\n\n**Files that touch the model types** (the blast radius of moving them):\n`heca/src/actions.rs`, `app/interaction.rs`, `app/registry.rs`, `chrome/context_menu.rs`,\n`chrome/layers.rs`, `chrome/mod.rs`, `chrome/overlay.rs`, `chrome/realize.rs`, `chrome/view.rs`,\n`handlers.rs`, `keymap.rs`.\n\n**CORRECTION, measured 2026-07-27 while doing the work:** only **four** import lines name the\n`view` module path directly (`chrome/realize.rs:45`, `chrome/overlay.rs:24`, `:29`, `:445`). The\nother files reach the types through `chrome`'s own re-export, so re-pointing that one re-export at\n`heca_view` covers them. And there is **ONE** production caller of `realize`, not two:\n`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs:371`. `chrome/mod.rs` only re-exports it.\n\n# THE KEY INSIGHT THAT MAKES THIS SMALL\n\n**`realize` only ever constructs ONE `InteractionIntent` variant: `View(intent)`.** It never touches\n`ActivateAction`, `FocusPane`, `FocusWorkspace` or any other. So `realize` does not depend on the\napp's intent model — it depends on *being able to hand back an intent*. The coupling is a **wrapper\nat the boundary, not a real dependency**.\n\n# ⚠️ THE WRINKLE — CHECKED 2026-07-27, DO NOT ASSUME OTHERWISE\n\nI first guessed the hint registry could simply become `Intent`-keyed. **It cannot.**\n`HintTargetRegistry` stores `InteractionIntent` and is **shared**: `heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs`\nregisters modal action buttons carrying `InteractionIntent::ActivateAction(WmAction::SubmitOverlay\n{..})`, which is not a `View` intent. So the registry must keep storing `InteractionIntent` to serve\nthe app's own callers.\n\n**Therefore `realize` needs a narrower seam than the concrete registry** — the same shape as the\nemitter:\n\n- **emit:** `Rc<dyn Fn(Intent)>` over the *model's* `Intent`. `heca` supplies a closure that wraps it\n  as `InteractionIntent::View(..)`.\n- **register a hint target:** a callback (or small trait) `FnMut(Intent) -> HintTargetId`. `heca`\n  supplies a closure that wraps and calls its existing `HintTargetRegistry::register`. The registry\n  itself is UNCHANGED and keeps serving overlay.\n\n`HintTargetId` already lives in `heca-grid-ui` (`heca-grid-ui/src/hint.rs:22`), which is below —\nnothing to move there.\n\n# THE WORK, IN ORDER\n\n1. **New crate `heca-view`.** Move `heca/src/chrome/view.rs` into it wholesale. Add it to the\n   workspace members and to `heca`'s dependencies. Fix imports — mechanical, compiler-guided.\n2. **Flip the two seams.** Change `realize`'s `emit` to take the model `Intent`, and replace\n   `hints: &mut HintTargetRegistry` with the register callback/trait. Wrap at the `heca` boundary in\n   the one production caller (`chrome/overlay.rs:371`). Only ~7 sites inside realize construct the\n   carrier.\n3. **Move `realize` down** into **`heca-view-realize`** (deps: `heca-view`, `heca-grid-ui`,\n   `heca-theme`) — the two-crate split decided above. `FormBindings` moves with it. Its ~1500-line\n   test module moves too.\n4. **Prove it: a showcase demo that renders a described tree.** This is the point of the whole task\n   — without it, Level 2 has bought nothing observable. Show a `ViewNode` tree with a `Panel`, a\n   `Row` with a press intent, a `Separator` and a colour override, side by side with the native\n   equivalents.\n\n# RISK\n\n**Low.** This is a move, not a redesign: the compiler catches every miss, and the workspace has 20\ngreen test suites guarding behaviour. The cost is **bulk, not danger**.\n\n# EFFORT\n\n**One focused session** with full context — comparable to F003/P010/T006 (the action-argument\ndeclarations) plus crate plumbing. Explicitly NOT started on 2026-07-27 because that session was at\n~69% context and a multi-file crate move is the worst thing to run out of context partway through.\n\n# ALSO IN SCOPE ONCE THIS LANDS (mentioned in the original task text)\n\n- A plugin written in JavaScript or Python still gets no Rust completion. Because the vocabulary is\n  a CLOSED list with a coverage guard already walking it (`WidgetKind::ALL`), matching definitions\n  for other languages could be **generated** from that same list. Nobody has costed this.\n  Tracked separately as **F003/P001/T006**.\n- Check that F003/P017/T003's generated property tables are reusable rather than private to the app\n  — they are the natural source for those generated definitions.\n- **F003/P011/T006** (\"typed builder SDK over ViewNode\") says \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\". With the\n  model inside the app that sentence could not be true of anything; after this task it can be.\n\n# ACCEPTANCE\n\n- The model lives in its own crate, depending on nothing app-side.\n- `realize` is callable from below `heca`, with the emitter and hint-target registration passed in\n  rather than reaching into app types.\n- `heca`'s production caller wraps at the boundary; `HintTargetRegistry` is unchanged and still\n  serves overlay's non-`View` intents.\n- **The showcase renders a described tree**, and the USER looks at it — that is the whole point.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n# ✅ DONE 2026-07-27 — Level 2 shipped, verified in the app by the user (\"looks good\")\n\nSix commits on `feat/action-arg-declaration`. Whole workspace green (**961 tests, 24 suites**),\nclippy 0 warnings at every commit. Nothing pushed.\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `a81f068` | **`heca-view`** — the model moves out of the app. `serde` only, no widget library, no renderer, no taffy. |\n| `f098e99` | `realize` takes **seams** instead of app types: `IntentEmitter` (`Rc<dyn Fn(Intent)>`) + the `HintTargets` trait. |\n| `8519db4` | **`heca-view-realize`** — the mapper moves below the app. |\n| `541c479` | The showcase renders a described tree beside its hand-built twin. |\n| `01f14c8` | `fix(row)`: a state highlight can no longer be shorter than its content (found by looking). |\n| `d1eb204` | The demo rows get padding, like every other row on the page. |\n\n## Crate layout, as decided\n\n- **`heca-view`** — `ViewNode`, `WidgetKind`, `PropValue`, `Intent`, `PropMap`, `ViewSize`,\n  `ViewVariant`, `ViewAlign`, `Events`. Dep: `serde` (+ `serde_json` for its tests).\n- **`heca-view-realize`** — `realize`, `FormBindings`, `IntentEmitter`, `HintTargets`. Deps:\n  `heca-view`, `heca-grid-ui`, `serde`, `serde_json` (+ `heca-core` for tests). Note: `heca-theme`\n  turned out NOT to be needed — `Theme` is re-exported by `heca-grid-ui`.\n- `heca` depends on both; `heca-renderer` takes both as **dev**-dependencies for the showcase.\n\n## The app side of the seams (where to look)\n\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` — re-exports the model from `heca_view` and the mapper from\n  `heca_view_realize`, so the app still has one path to the vocabulary. `ViewHintTargets<'a>` lives\n  here, next to `HintTargetRegistry`: it is the only thing that knows both an `Intent` and an\n  `InteractionIntent`.\n- `heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs` (`build_modal_root`) — the one production caller. It wraps the\n  emitter in a closure and the registry in `ViewHintTargets`.\n- `HintTargetRegistry` is **unchanged** and still stores `InteractionIntent`, because overlay\n  registers `ActivateAction(SubmitOverlay)` in the same map. That was the wrinkle; the seam is the\n  one operation realize performs on it.\n\n## Two measurements in the old plan were wrong — corrected here\n\n- **ONE** production caller of `realize`, not two. `chrome/mod.rs` only re-exported it.\n- **FOUR** import lines named the `view` module path, not eleven files. Everything else reached the\n  types through `chrome`'s re-export, so re-pointing that one re-export covered them.\n\n## Dead code the move surfaced\n\n`map_align` (`ViewAlign` → grid-ui `Align`) had been redundant since alignment became an ordinary\nproperty travelling by name onto `Layout`; the app's module-wide `allow(dead_code)` hid it. Deleted,\nwith a note where it stood pointing at `grid_alignment_is_authorable_on_both_axes`. The one\nremaining narrow allow is on `WidgetKind::ordinal`, which must stay **compiled** in every build\nbecause its exhaustive match is what makes an unlisted variant a compile error.\n\nTests were conserved exactly across the move: heca's 422 unit tests became **374 + 48**.\n\n## The widget defect the showcase found (this is why step 4 mattered)\n\nThe hover/active pill was drawn inset 3px unconditionally, so a row whose content reaches its own\nedges got a pill **shorter than its content** — the badge stuck out above and below. Fixed in the\nlibrary, not the call site:\n\n- `Base::highlight_rect(inset)` (`heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs`) — the inset may only spend space\n  the widget's own padding already reserves, per side. Every widget drawing an inset highlight asks\n  here.\n- `Item` had the identical arithmetic with a 4px inset and the same latent bug — same call now.\n- `Layout::pad_left/pad_right/pad_top/pad_bottom` (`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs`) — the per-side\n  padding cascade had been inline in `to_taffy`; paint needs the same numbers, so it has one home\n  and `to_taffy` reads it.\n- Guard: `a_state_highlight_never_crops_the_content_it_covers` in\n  `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs`. Confirmed by restoring the old arithmetic and watching it fail\n  (3.0 vs 0.0 on the unpadded row).\n\n**Second report, measured not guessed:** the remaining \"badge overflows\" was the badge's *glow*\n(`GLOW_RADIUS = 10.0`), which paints outside its box by design — row 37px, badge box 35px centred\ninside it. Nothing left to fix in the library; the demo rows were simply the only rows on the page\nwritten without padding, and now carry 6px. Noted for whoever writes the next demo: 6px does not\nfully contain a 10px halo, and that is expected.\n\n## Follow-ups this unblocks (not done here)\n\n- **F003/P001/T006** — generated widget definitions for JS/Python from `WidgetKind::ALL`.\n- **F003/P011/T006** — \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\" can now be true of `heca-view`.\n- Check whether F003/P017/T003's generated property tables are reusable outside the app.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
